{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## 2026-11-02: ENV_ID_MISMATCH root cause measured; implementation of option (2) paused for a design input\n\nReproduced read-only against the live store with `EnvAuthorshipTally` + `env_identity.divergence_report` (the exact fsck path, `fsck_tracker_health._tracker_health`).\n\n**What drives the finding.** `divergence_report` keys authors by the free-text `author` display name. The 3 env ids are sequential, not concurrent: ade0f2ef 2026-06-26..08-09 PDT, b8a354e0 08-09..09-10 PDT, 492a5c71 09-14 PDT..now. The bot's display name on this host is \"Rebar Bot Nava\"; on the older envs it is \"RebarBotNava\". Those strings differ, so the bot never overlaps. The only overlapping author is **\"Joe Oakhart\"**: 8 events on 492a5c71 (09-14..09-20, email joeoakhart@navapbc.com, no author_id) vs 1358 on ade0f2ef and 4549 on b8a354e0 (a mix of the bot email + bot author_id 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d and the human email).\n\n**Consequence for option (2).** Skipping the bot by display name changes nothing on this store. Re-keying by identity (author_id, else email) and skipping identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d still leaves joeoakhart@navapbc.com under both 492a5c71 and b8a354e0, so fsck still reports ENV_ID_MISMATCH. Under the decision, other authors keep the check, so that remaining line would need its own justification (AC6) or another decision.\n\n**No existing source names the shared bot identity.** Checked: the `[identity]` config section (only require_authenticated, signing_key, enforce_since), the identity ticket 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d (no tag or field marks it as shared), rebar.toml, and the bot email in source (only `BRIDGE_BOT_EMAIL`, a CI-runner env var read by `_bridge_runner`, not available to fsck on a dev host). Implementing the skip needs a new mechanism, such as a config key or an identity-ticket marker. Per instructions, no code was written; options are reported to the operator.\n\nWorktree `.rebar/worktrees/fix-esok-envid` is provisioned at origin/main b2dca9bf5ea, with no changes."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793670313332766317,"uuid":"e2155894-7e30-43d6-92a8-27d5fe00edfa"}